    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43725" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔεικτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>pliant, tractable</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				69.20
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Zonar.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔοικτος</span> (q. v.) codd.);
				<i>soft, yielding</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ
			εὔ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Aphr.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				2.23
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Heraclit.
				<u>All.</u>
				51
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔθικτος</span> codd.); of
			abscesses, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				4.18
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ότερος</span>, 
				gloss on 
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λειότερος</span>
			, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				49.3.5
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τως
				</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τῶς</span> cod.) 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐεκτικῶς</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
